"""history_out_of_read_path_v1_20261021.py -- escalation #2183 (option C of the #2179 review, as
widened by the researcher; element of the IBA app reset, #2177).

Researcher, 2026-10-21, verbatim: "History that are replaced with a new or changed version, in
every file or document or table must be handled in such a way that it is not read every time and
is only kept for deliberate read to assess a historic status."

Config:
  - new cfg_behaviour_rule (documentation) replaced-history-out-of-read-path
  - rule 33 (single-living-register-update-in-place): "struck through or annotated" replaced
  - governance.governance_md_on_rule_change: GOVERNANCE.md describes the mechanism now; a single
    rule change is recorded in cfg_change_detail, not as a GOVERNANCE.md entry
  - live rule texts and governance settings that carried their own change history (dated
    amendments, incident accounts, superseded wording) restated as the current rule only. For a
    behaviour rule the removed text is appended to its `source`; for a setting the prior value is
    in cfg_change_detail (before_json), the setting's history home.
  - cfg_control_home 'mechanism': history_home names the archived GOVERNANCE.md.

Every write through configmaint.apply_logged(). Idempotent (a row already holding its target text
is skipped). One transaction.

Usage:
    python iba/app/migration/history_out_of_read_path_v1_20261021.py [--db PATH] [--dry-run]
"""
